# 04. DECISION

**Document 02 remains the canonical domain vocabulary.**

**Document 06 remains the concrete data architecture.**

Document 06 must therefore be interpreted as a **data-layer specialization and decomposition of the canonical domain model**, not as a replacement for it.

This means:

```text
DOMAIN MODEL
     ↓
Canonical business concepts
     ↓
DATA MODEL
     ↓
Concrete persisted/queryable representations
```

The data layer may contain more granular entities than the domain layer when those entities provide necessary implementation detail.

---

# 05. DOMAIN VS DATA DISTINCTION

AEGIS must distinguish between:

### Domain Concept

What the system means.

### Data Entity

How the system stores, transports, indexes, or queries information.

### UI Representation

How the concept is presented to the user.

### API Resource

How the concept is exposed through a service boundary.

These are related but are not required to have identical names.

---

# 06. CANONICAL MAPPING RULE

The following principle is mandatory:

> **A more granular data entity must map to a canonical domain concept.**

No data entity may become an independent domain concept merely because it has its own database table or API endpoint.

